It relies on, but does not include, the following third-party software and models:

- Hugging Face Transformers (Apache-2.0). smel/layer_runner.py re-executes, at runtime, the source of
  `torch_chunk_gated_delta_rule` from the installed transformers package as a pure-PyTorch reference;
  no transformers code is copied into this repository.
- flash-linear-attention / fla-core (MIT): Gated DeltaNet kernels.
- llama.cpp / ggml (MIT): GGUF quantization through the user's own build (ggml_quantize_chunk),
  gguf-py for reading and writing GGUF files.
  inference/llama_cpp_patches/mixed-experts-b11827.patch is a modification of llama.cpp (build b11827,
  commit 970b51ce7, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors) and is distributed under llama.cpp's MIT license.
- Qwen3.6-35B-A3B by the Qwen team (Apache-2.0): the base model; weights and tokenizer are downloaded
  by the user from the Hugging Face Hub and are not redistributed here.
- Gemma 4 26B A4B by Google (Apache-2.0): the second supported base model; weights and tokenizer are
  downloaded by the user from the Hugging Face Hub and are not redistributed here.

Ideas adapted from the authors' own Soup Kernel Challenge solution (Apache-2.0, not copied verbatim; rewritten
for SMEL FT's frozen norms, chunked head and own LoRA): the fused RMSNorm and residual-add + RMSNorm kernels
(smel/norm.py), the single-pass chunked cross-entropy with the gradient taken in the same pass (smel/loss.py,
_ce_chunk), the LoRA add as the epilogue of its GEMM and the shared gate/up input (smel/lora.py), the recompile
check (tests/test_recompile.py) and the GPU-idle analysis of a profiler trace (scripts/bench/trace_gaps.py).
